  "verdict_text": "Spec: No blocking findings. `WorkflowInput.admission_report` preserves the original doctor for v1–v6; v7 checks frozen inventory/planner selections and work/review members. MCP availability is conditional on selected MCP modes. `_Submission.dispatch` retains native policy, trusted checks, connection, shared claim and transport ownership, with overrides restored in `finally`. Unknown recovery uses the original input and memo without invoking admission or resending.\n\nStandards: No blocking findings. Backend construction and command behavior remain with the existing backend owner. Codex availability and command construction share `executable()`, and configuration validation reuses `_options`. The candidate adds no scheduler or journal. Tests reuse the durable SDK fixture and exercise meaningful admission/recovery boundaries. No consequential redundant guard, test duplication or performance defect was found.\n\nComplete scope read:\n\n- `src/ergora/agent_backends.py`\n- `src/ergora/reference_inputs.py`\n- `src/ergora/reference_task_submission.py`\n- `tests/fixtures/task_submission_client.py`\n- `tests/test_issue_submission.py`\n- `tests/test_task_submission.py`\n- `src/ergora/processes.py`\n- `src/ergora/data/reference/platform/local/agent_platform/doctor.py`\n- `src/ergora/data/reference/platform/local/agent_platform/cli.py`\n- `src/ergora/data/reference/platform/local/agent_platform/sandbox.py`\n- `docs/plans/2026-11-11-source-task-admission.md`\n- `docs/delivery/2026-11-11-source-task-admission.md`\n\nBoth ancestor instructions and both Skills were read completely through task MCP. All 123,194 candidate bytes were read as continuous UTF-8 pages through `next_offset: null`. No shell, network, writes or test execution occurred.\n\nEvidence limits: The reported r2 25-test run and separate legacy boundary retest do not establish a complete r2 suite result. The deterministic six-stage journey establishes r1 success-path evidence. The ongoing r2 hybrid journey establishes no completed outcome, distinct-backend success or model-quality result. Wheel/frozen-file identities were reported, not independently recomputed here; final delivery acceptance remains outside this structural verdict.",
